version 0.11
symbol c-pol

description Polarized capacitor, 2-pin generic view
tags capacitor polarized tantalum
pin_numbers hide
pin_names hide
# Polarized capacitor view, US convention: the positive pin (1) ends on a straight plate, the negative pin (2) ends on
# an arc whose middle leans toward that plate (its ends splay away), and a plus sign sits above the straight plate.
# Pin connection points sit on the 0.5 mm placement lattice (ADR-0074); the tails and the body follow it where that is convenient.
field Reference at=[0,2.5] U
field Value at=[0,-2.5] c-pol

pins
  1  [-4,0]  0    length=3
  2  [4,0]   180  length=3.5

body
  arc   [1,-1.5,0.5,0,1,1.5]     width=0.25
  line  [-1,-1.5,-1,1.5]         width=0.25
  line  [-1.5,1.5,-1.5,2]        width=0.25
  line  [-1.75,1.75,-1.25,1.75]  width=0.25
